		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=790#p790"><![CDATA[
A new Bullet source distribution is available (April 4, 2006)<br><br>Latest changes are:<br><br>- CcdPhysicsDemo has mouse dragging, as requested by Oliver S.<br>- New Build System, thanks to Frank Richter<br>- 3D Sweep and Prune, thanks to Simon Hobbs<br>- Improved stability in the Iterative Impulse Solver, thanks to Erin Catto (see his GDC 2006 paper at <a href="http://www.gphysics.com" class="postlink">http://www.gphysics.com</a>)<br><br><a href="http://bullet.sourceforge.net" class="postlink">http://bullet.sourceforge.net</a><br><br>Source zipfile:<br><a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pub/test/index.php?dir=physics/source/&amp;file=bullet-1.2src.zip" class="postlink">http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pu ... 1.2src.zip</a><br><br>A win32 demo:<br><a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pub/test/index.php?dir=physics/&amp;file=bullet1.2_demo.zip" class="postlink">http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pu ... 2_demo.zip</a><br><br><br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Tue Mar 21, 2006 4:36 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
